guide forever/horde/30-40/03-arathi-highlands
title Arathi Highlands, Badlands & The Barrens
faction Horde
levels 37-40
zone Arathi Highlands
next forever/horde/30-40/04-dustwallow-marsh

# Consensus route (Horde, simulator export consensus-horde-tauren), visits
# 25-28 of the export it was written from: Arathi Highlands 37.4-38.4,
# Hillsbrad Foothills (Tarren Mill), Badlands 38.4-39.2, The Barrens 39.2.
# The October refresh's export (visits 23-27) runs Arathi 37.4-38.5, the
# Barrens 38.5, Dustwallow Marsh, Tarren Mill 39.2 and then the Badlands
# 39.2-40; this guide keeps the Badlands right after Arathi, where the
# Thandol Span road already leads, and Dustwallow follows in the next guide.
# Shared by every Horde start. Era + known Forever quests only.
#
# Flow: fly Booty Bay -> Grom'gol, zeppelin to the Undercity (training;
# Hunters and Shamans train in Orgrimmar, Druids in Thunder Bluff, on the
# way there), fly to Tarren
# Mill -> ride into Arathi: the Boulderfist camp -> the Shards of Myzrael ->
# Hammerfall (flight path, bind) -> raptor eyes outside the walls -> Hammerfall -> Drywhisker
# Gorge and the Stone of East Binding -> Witherbark Village -> Fleshstalker
# raptors -> Faldir's Cove -> the Stone of Outer Binding, Northfold Manor, the
# Stone of West Binding -> the Stone of Inner Binding -> hearth to Hammerfall
# -> Boulderfist Hall -> Hammerfall -> Thandol Span, the Wetlands and Loch
# Modan road into the Badlands -> Valley of Fangs -> the Dustbowl -> Kargath
# (flight path, bind) -> rock elementals -> coyotes, buzzards and the Greater
# Rock Elementals -> Kargath -> the Dustbowl -> Valley of Fangs -> Agmond's
# End -> the Ancient Chest -> Agmond's End -> hearth to Kargath -> fly to
# Grom'gol -> zeppelin to Orgrimmar (train; Druids and Paladins in Thunder
# Bluff) -> fly to the Crossroads -> the
# Forgotten Pools -> the Crossroads -> fly to Ratchet (bind).
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Visit 26 (Tarren Mill) is dropped as a stop: Blackmoore's Legacy (506)
#   is turned in to Krusk in forever/horde/30-40/01-desolace, right after
#   Strahnbrad, and Baron Vardus (566) is never turned in. Tarren Mill is
#   only the landing point: Booty Bay's flight master reaches only Grom'gol
#   from here, so you fly there, take the zeppelin to the Undercity and fly
#   from the Undercity to Tarren Mill (Hammerfall's flight path is not known
#   yet), then ride east into Arathi. The export's Tarren
#   Mill bind is dropped: Kargath replaces it before use.
# - The Hammerfall flight path and bind (taken at the end of the export's
#   Stranglethorn visit) are taken here, on arrival.
# - Arathi is one loop from Hammerfall: the Myzrael shards, Drywhisker Gorge
#   and the East Binding key first (all beside Hammerfall), then south and
#   west around the highlands, so the three keys are picked up in passing.
#   The Hammer May Fall (676) is killed on the ride in and turned in on
#   arrival.
# - Badlands: Rigglefuzz's Barbecued Buzzard Wings (703) is taken when the
#   road passes the Valley of Fangs, not after the elementals. The export's
#   mid-visit hearth to Kargath is used at the end of the Badlands instead,
#   from Agmond's End.
# - The Crossroads bind is dropped: the Ratchet bind replaces it the same
#   hour.
# - Class training added at about 37.5 (the Undercity, or Orgrimmar and
#   Thunder Bluff for the classes the Undercity cannot train) and in
#   Orgrimmar at 38-39 (Thunder Bluff for Druids and Paladins), on the way
#   through.
#
# Left out (accepted by the export, never turned in): WANTED: Baron Vardus
# (566), Pearl Diving (705), Uldaman Reagent Run (2202), To the Undercity for
# Yagyin's Digest (728), The Swarm Grows (1145). Dragonmaw Rumors (95663) is
# no longer in the refreshed export. Also left out: Outrider Basic Care
# Package (7866, 270 XP), which the export takes at the Mor'shan Rampart: a
# detour to the far north of the Barrens isn't worth it.
# Added in the October refresh (Forever above 30 cannot be checked in game
# until launch on 4 November: from the data, not from play): The Kolkar of
# Desolace (1362), now accepted from Regthar Deathgate and turned in at
# Ghost Walker Post in forever/horde/30-40/04-dustwallow-marsh, as the new
# export does.
# PvP, left out: the Darkspear Islands battleground quests, The Battle for
# Darkspear Islands! (98906, Nizook Boof by Ratchet), which the new export
# takes here, and Conflict at Darkspear Islands (98887, 98888, the Horde
# Warbringer at the Mor'shan Rampart): each needs a battleground win or
# marks of honor, which a solo leveling route does not plan for.
# Optional: Stone Is Better than Cloth (716) needs Patterned Bronze Bracers
# (Blacksmithing or the Auction House). Study of the Elements: Rock (712):
# its Greater Rock Elementals are 42-44, four or five levels above you, and
# the bracers drop one kill in five.
# Dropped: This Must Be The Place (79976): the Messenger Bag only offers it
# after Eagle's Fist (79975), the end of the Cozy Sleeping Bag chain that no
# Horde guide runs.
# Crystal in the Mountains (635) and Trollbane (638) are accepted in the
# Stranglethorn guide; their turn-ins here are skipped if you never had them.
# Restored: Martek the Exiled (1106, Fizzle's letter, accepted at the
# Shimmering Flats in forever/horde/07-ashenvale) and Indurium (1108): the
# Stonevault troggs sit between the Valley of Fangs and Agmond's End, on the
# loop already made. Sunken Treasure (669) is carried to Fleet Master
# Seahorn, turned in at Booty Bay in forever/horde/40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale.
# Skipped: Sunken Treasure part 6 (670) and Death From Below (667): 670 is
# taken from Seahorn only after 669, around level 40, and both end at
# Faldir's Cove, which the route has left by then: a trip back to Arathi.
#
# Class quests:
# - Warlock: the Felhunter is in forever/class/warlock/felhunter-horde (its
#   Undercity, Wetlands and Ratchet steps left this guide for it).
# - Warrior: The Islander (1718) from Sorek in Orgrimmar, The Affray (1719)
#   on Fray Island, a short ride south of Ratchet: Berserker Stance. It waits
#   for this point because Big Will is level 33. The follow-ups (The
#   Windwatcher 1791, Cyclonian 1712) end in an elite fight: they are in the
#   Warrior class guide Whirlwind Weapon.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tarren Mill

step Fly to Grom'gol
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip From Booty Bay, fly to Grom'gol. The Undercity zeppelin leaves from the tower on the west side of the camp.
  fly "Grom'gol"
  goto 31.5,29.4 "Zeppelin to the Undercity"

step Orgrimmar
  only Hunter,Shaman
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip The Undercity has no Hunter or Shaman trainer: take the Orgrimmar zeppelin from the same tower instead and train in the city, then take the Undercity zeppelin from the tower outside Orgrimmar's main gate.
  train class

step Thunder Bluff
  only Druid
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Cast Teleport: Moonglade and take Bunthen Plainswind's flight to Thunder Bluff; Turak Runetotem trains you on Elder Rise. Then fly to Orgrimmar and take the Undercity zeppelin from the tower outside the main gate.
  train class

step Undercity trainers
  only Warrior,Paladin,Rogue,Priest,Mage,Warlock
  zone Undercity
  tip Train while you are in the Undercity: the trainers stand in the War Quarter, the Rogues' Quarter and the Magic Quarter (Paladins: Garen Largo).
  train class

step Fly to Tarren Mill
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip The zeppelin lands at the towers outside the Undercity: head down into the city and fly to Tarren Mill.
  fly "Tarren Mill"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Into Arathi

step Boulderfist camp
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Head east out of Tarren Mill through Thoradin's Wall and follow the road east. The Boulderfist Ogres and Enforcers (32-34) camp south of the road, south-east of Northfold Manor.
  kill 2562 quest 676.1
  kill 2564 quest 676.2

step The Shards of Myzrael
  tip The violet shards glow just off the road a short way west of Hammerfall.
  turnin 635
  accept 642

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Hammerfall

step Hammerfall
  tip The orc stronghold at the eastern end of the road. Urda, the wind rider master, stands by the gate.
